VERDICT: REJECTED
The changes do not fully satisfy the stated objective because removing `plugins/start.py` broke core behavior required by one of the kept features (`broadcast`).

Critical findings:
- `start.py` previously contained the only call sites that registered users/chats in DB (`db.add_user`, `db.add_chat`). After this diff, there are no remaining call sites for either across the codebase.
- `broadcast.py` relies on `db.get_chats()` / `db.get_users()` as its recipient source. With no registration path, fresh deployments will have empty recipient lists and broadcast becomes non-functional.
- This is a functional regression in a plugin category that was explicitly intended to be kept.

Security: none observed.

Next actions:
1. Reintroduce a minimal registration path (e.g., lightweight handler for bot-added-to-group and private user onboarding) so chats/users are persisted.
2. Re-test broadcast end-to-end on a clean DB to confirm recipients are discovered and messages send.
3. OptVERDICT: REJECTED
ionally keep plugin cleanup, but ensure removed commands/features do not remove shared lifecycle hooks needed by retained features.

